Title: Link winwrap into the standalone node.exe for Windows XP
Origin: electron-legacy (this repo)

Only reached when building Node on its own. Electron compiles the same libuv,
V8 and src/ through GN and does not read node.gyp, so this is inert there --
the same arrangement as 04-node-version-check-winxp.patch.

Two settings, both on the node executable rather than on node_lib or on every
target in the tree.

The dependency and /INCLUDE: belong at the final link because that is where
the __imp_<name> slots are resolved, and it is the link kernel32.lib is also
on. Without the anchor the redirect table is an archive member nothing
references: kernel32 satisfies every slot first, the member is never
extracted, and the build succeeds while redirecting nothing. winwrap.gyp has
the long version, including why /WHOLEARCHIVE is not the answer.

Not applied to cctest or the embedtests: those run on the build machine, and
giving them the anchor without the library is LNK2001.

MinimumRequiredVersion is the other half. winwrap supplies the imports XP
lacks; the subsystem version is what lets XP's loader accept the binary at
all. 5.01 and 5.02 are as low as the linker goes for each machine.

winwrap itself is fetched into deps/winwrap by build_node.sh.

diff --git a/node.gyp b/node.gyp
--- a/node.gyp
+++ b/node.gyp
@@ -592,8 +592,51 @@
         '<(node_lib_target_name)',
       ],
 
+      'conditions': [
+        ['OS=="win"', {
+          # winwrap supplies the Win32 functions XP does not export, by
+          # defining the __imp_<name> slots the call sites load through. It has
+          # to be linked into the executable rather than into node_lib: the
+          # slots are resolved at the final link, and that is where kernel32
+          # would otherwise satisfy them.
+          #
+          # Only this target, not every executable in the tree. cctest and the
+          # embedtests are developer tools that run on the build machine, and
+          # giving them the /INCLUDE: below without the library would be
+          # LNK2001.
+          'dependencies': [
+            'deps/winwrap/winwrap.gyp:winwrap',
+          ],
+        }],
+      ],
+
       'msvs_settings': {
         'VCLinkerTool': {
+          'conditions': [
+            # The subsystem version is the other half of running on XP:
+            # winwrap supplies the imports, this is what lets the loader
+            # accept the binary at all. 5.01 for Win32 and 5.02 for x64,
+            # which is as low as the linker goes for each machine.
+            #
+            # /INCLUDE: names winwrap's anchor, which forces the redirect
+            # table into the link. Without it the table is an archive member
+            # nothing references: kernel32.lib is on this link line too, so it
+            # resolves every __imp_<name> first and the member is never
+            # extracted -- a clean build that redirects nothing. The symbol
+            # takes the usual decoration, hence the leading underscore on x86.
+            ['target_arch=="ia32"', {
+              'MinimumRequiredVersion': '5.01',
+              'AdditionalOptions': [
+                '/INCLUDE:_winwrap_static_redirects',
+              ],
+            }],
+            ['target_arch=="x64"', {
+              'MinimumRequiredVersion': '5.02',
+              'AdditionalOptions': [
+                '/INCLUDE:winwrap_static_redirects',
+              ],
+            }],
+          ],
           'GenerateMapFile': 'true', # /MAP
           'MapExports': 'true', # /MAPINFO:EXPORTS
           'RandomizedBaseAddress': 2, # enable ASLR
